# M6 4a (slice 345; Codex CODEX-OPUS-345-4A-REPLY-20261110T041147Z-01 item 3): a named actual whose tail is a Structure
# of written fields (`a: y: 6`) for the int formal a -- the ordinary refusal of admission when the call is reached (4),
# no special rule for the number of fields; `before` is computed, `after` never.
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a 2) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
int: before 1
int: r tst(a: y: 6)
int: after before + 1
